{
  "$comment": "Personal overrides for Claude Code. Copy to settings.local.json (gitignored). The Claude Code harness authenticates via `claude login` — do not put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here, that silently switches the harness to API billing. The application reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from .env (see env.example). To re-enable curl locally, add \"Bash(curl:*)\" to permissions.allow below. `Bash(curl *)`/`Bash(wget *)` are NOT denied by default (python:* isn't either, so a Bash-permission deny gave a false sense of coverage) — for real egress control, especially on autonomous/unattended runs, add a `sandbox` block restricting network access by domain, e.g.: `\"sandbox\": {\"network\": {\"allowedDomains\": [\"api.anthropic.com\", \"github.com\", \"*.githubusercontent.com\", \"pypi.org\", \"files.pythonhosted.org\"], \"strictAllowlist\": true}}`. Tune the domain list to what this project's tooling actually calls (add your Jira host, npm/pnpm registry, etc. if used) — there is no one-size-fits-all list, which is why it isn't enabled by default.",
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(open:*)"
    ]
  }
}
